                  <provenance type="#i" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_537">Syon,
                        Middlesex. Bridgettine abbey of St Saviour, St Mary the Virgin, and St
                        Bridget</orgName><p>On flyleaf: <q><persName role="fmo">Elisabeth
                              Arychley</persName> off Syon 13 Ian anno 1521</q>.</p><p>[Note on data
                        history: it appears that this Syon attribution was erroneously labelled as a
                        reject in the index to the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                        Britain (1964), p. 341; compare the main entry on p. 185].</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_333">London, London,
                        Dominican convent</orgName>
                     <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                        Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card recorded the
                        following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution
                        [and there is a later question mark above the word <q>freers</q>]:</p>
                     <p><q>Jasper Fyloll of the blacke freers in London oweth this booke [etc]</q>.
                        [M. R. James compares the Romance of Alexander, MS Bodley 264, fol.
                        1v].</p><p> Fyllol was an agent of Thomas Cromwell (cf. Wright,
                           <title>Letters relating to the Suppresion</title>, p. 67). One Fillow
                        appears among donors in the Syon catalogue: but this is probably too early
                        for him to be Jasper.</p></provenance>
               </history>
